course: dictionary
lesson: 12872
title: Enrich: making things better
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Enrich» means to make something better, fuller or more interesting by adding something good to it. When a trip takes you to a museum, it enriches your learning. The word is about adding something good, not taking anything away.
explain: «Reading every day enriches your vocabulary.» Each book you read adds new words to what you already know. Look at the word: it is built from rich, so it is about making something richer, in a good way.
explain: In science, enrich means to add useful things to soil, food or a substance. «The flour was enriched with iron» means iron was added to make it healthier. «Compost enriches the soil» means compost adds food that helps plants grow. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning you need.
fact: Enrich means to make something better, fuller or more interesting by adding something good to it.
fact: «A trip to the museum enriches learning» means the trip makes learning richer and more interesting.
fact: In science, enrich means to add useful things, such as vitamins added to «enriched flour».
fact: «Compost enriches the soil» means compost adds food that helps plants grow.
fact: Enrich can also mean to make someone richer with money, and in stories it can mean getting rich in an unfair way.
exercise: «Reading every day enriches your vocabulary.» What does enrich mean here? | Makes your vocabulary smaller | Makes you forget your words | *Makes your vocabulary better and fuller | Makes your book heavier
exercise: «Compost enriches the soil.» Why would a gardener do this? | To wash the soil away | To hide the soil under stones | To make the soil dry and hard | *To help the plants grow better
exercise: A food label says «enriched with vitamins». What has been done to the food? | The food has gone sour | *Useful vitamins have been added | Vitamins have been taken out | The food has been cooked for longer
test: «A museum trip can ___ your learning.» Which word fits the gap? | forget | *enrich | close | shrink
test: «The farmer enriched the soil with compost.» What did the farmer do? | *Added something useful to the soil | Watered the path | Took all the compost away | Dug a hole and filled it with sand
exam: Which sentence uses enrich in the science sense of adding something useful? | *«The flour was enriched with iron.» | «The flour was thrown in the bin.» | «The flour was emptied of all its iron.» | «The flour was sieved in the park.»
